      "content": "In your example, since `customer_name` and `customer_email` depend only on `customer_id` (not directly on `order_id`), this represents a transitive dependency, moving it out of 3NF violation. To fix this, you split the table into two: an `Orders` table with (`order_id`, `customer_id`) and a `Customers` table with (`customer_id`, `customer_name`, `customer_email`). This ensures customer details are stored only once in the dedicated customer table.",
      "source": "target",
